# SuperCool Finances: every endpoint as a ready-to-run request.
# Works with the VS Code REST Client and the JetBrains HTTP Client. The guide is docs/api/README.md.
#
# 1. Start the stack and seed it:  docker compose up --build --wait && make seed
# 2. Print the variables:           make demo-env
#    and paste TOKEN, OPERATOR_TOKEN, A and B into @token, @operatorToken, @accountA and @accountB.
#    Tokens are valid for 15 minutes.
# 3. Paste the ids that later requests need from earlier responses: @accountC from "Open an
#    account", @depositId from "Deposit", @transferId from "Transfer", @reversalId from "Reverse".
#
# Idempotency keys are fixed, so sending a request twice replays it (Idempotent-Replayed: true).
# Change the key to start a new operation.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-TOKEN-here
@operatorToken = paste-OPERATOR_TOKEN-here
@accountA = paste-A-here
@accountB = paste-B-here
@accountC = paste-the-id-of-the-opened-account-here
@depositId = paste-the-id-of-the-deposit-here
@transferId = paste-the-id-of-the-transfer-here
@reversalId = paste-the-id-of-the-reversal-here

### Liveness: the process runs (no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness: the database answers and every migration is applied (no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### OpenAPI document (no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs/json

### Open an account (customer; Idempotency-Key optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-open-cop-1

{"currency": "COP"}

### List your accounts, newest first (customer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read an account (customer: own accounts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read an account (operator: any customer account, with ownerId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

### Deposit 50.00 EUR (operator; Idempotency-Key required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-deposit-1

{"amount": "5000", "currency": "EUR"}

### Withdraw 20.00 EUR (customer, own account; Idempotency-Key required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-withdrawal-1

{"amount": "2000", "currency": "EUR"}

### Transfer 10.50 EUR from A to B (customer, own source; Idempotency-Key required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-transfer-1

{"destinationAccountId": "{{accountB}}", "amount": "1050", "currency": "EUR"}

### Read an account's history, newest first (customer or operator)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/entries?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read a transaction (customer: only the entries of their own accounts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/{{transferId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read a transaction (operator: every entry, settlement accounts included)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/{{depositId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

### Reverse the deposit (operator; Idempotency-Key required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/{{depositId}}/reversals
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-reversal-1

{"reason": "Deposit credited to the wrong account"}

### Read the reversal (operator)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/{{reversalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

### Freeze an account (operator; no body, no Idempotency-Key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountC}}/freeze
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

### Unfreeze it (operator)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountC}}/unfreeze
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

### Close it: only with balance "0", and final (operator)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountC}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

### Error: no token, 401 /problems/unauthenticated
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts

### Error: a customer deposits, 403 /problems/forbidden
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-forbidden-1

{"amount": "100", "currency": "EUR"}

### Error: another customer's account, 404 /problems/not-found
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountB}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error: no Idempotency-Key on a movement, 400 /problems/malformed-request
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "100", "currency": "EUR"}

### Error: an amount that is not minor units, 422 /problems/validation-error
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-validation-1

{"amount": "10.50", "currency": "EUR"}

### Error: the transfer's key with another body, 422 /problems/idempotency-key-reused
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-transfer-1

{"destinationAccountId": "{{accountB}}", "amount": "2000", "currency": "EUR"}

### Error: more than the balance, 422 /problems/insufficient-funds
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/{{accountA}}/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-insufficient-1

{"amount": "99999999", "currency": "EUR"}

### Error: the deposit reversed again, 409 /problems/already-reversed
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/{{depositId}}/reversals
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: http-reversal-2

{"reason": "Second attempt"}
